# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Single-maintainer repo today, but explicit ownership rules document
# which areas need extra care on review and route auto-requested
# reviews when more contributors arrive. Order matters — last matching
# pattern wins.

# Default: anything not matched below
*                                              @alsiola

# Infrastructure + CI/CD: changes here can break deploys or expose
# credentials. Always reviewed by infra owner.
/infra/                                        @alsiola
/.github/                                      @alsiola

# Auth + payments + safeguarding (incident reports): security and legal
# blast radius. Route to the relevant owner explicitly.
/apps/api/src/features/auth/                   @alsiola
/apps/api/src/features/payments/               @alsiola
/apps/api/src/features/incident-report/        @alsiola

# Database migrations: irreversible in prod (forward-only deploys).
/packages/db/src/migrations/                   @alsiola

# Architecture decision records: review for accuracy of "rejected
# alternatives" since they shape future decisions.
/docs/adrs/                                    @alsiola
